  "Semantic error, not-found, and permission-denied page with explicit recovery actions.": "Error semántico, página no encontrada y permiso denegado con acciones de recuperación explícitas.",
  "semantic heading": "encabezado semántico",
  "Semantic Nav Link": "Enlace de navegación semántica",
  "Semantic tone maps to the --gds-state-* role tokens, and the rule is deliberately not uniform: an alarm colour that moves is not an alarm, so danger is anchored, while tones that carry no urgency are tinted with the preset's own hue. Every figure below is counted from the resolved tokens at render time rather than written down, so this panel cannot fall out of step with the system it documents. The accent palette is separate: it never changes as you switch presets, because a category means the same thing in every theme. That is a contract, not a gap — a preset MAY declare its own accents, and the contrast gate then verifies that palette rather than the shared one.": "El tono semántico se asigna a los tokens de rol --gds-state-*, y la regla no es deliberadamente uniforme: un color de alarma que se mueve no es una alarma, por lo que el peligro está anclado, mientras que los tonos que no conllevan urgencia se tiñen con el propio tono preestablecido. Cada cifra a continuación se cuenta a partir de los tokens resueltos en el momento del renderizado en lugar de escribirse, por lo que este panel no puede desfasarse del sistema que documenta. La paleta de acento está separada: nunca cambia cuando cambias de ajustes preestablecidos, porque una categoría significa lo mismo en todos los temas. Eso es un contrato, no una brecha: un ajuste preestablecido PUEDE declarar sus propios acentos, y la puerta de contraste verifica esa paleta en lugar de la compartida.",
  "Semantic Vocabulary Extension Lane": "Carril de extensión del vocabulario semántico",
  "SemanticButton takes action=\"save\"|\"add\"|\"edit\"|... not free text": "SemanticButton toma acción=\"guardar\"|\"añadir\"|\"editar\"|... no texto libre",
  "SemanticButton's transient success/error treatment, live and clickable. Success feedback is per action — its own icon and message key, read from GdsVocabulary — so a delete confirms with its own glyph rather than a generic tick; error feedback is uniform. The revert duration is surfaced from GDS_BUTTON_FEEDBACK_DURATION_MS, the constant the component itself uses. Each action also declares a feedback colour; what paints depends on the active preset's governed Button rules, so the table reports the declaration and the live proof shows the rendering.": "SemanticButton's transient success/error treatment, live and clickable. Success feedback is per action — its own icon and message key, read from GdsVocabulary — so a delete confirms with its own glyph rather than a generic tick; error feedback is uniform. The revert duration is surfaced from GDS_BUTTON_FEEDBACK_DURATION_MS, the constant the component itself uses. Each action also declares a feedback colour; what paints depends on the active preset's governed Button rules, so the table reports the declaration and the live proof shows the rendering.",
